    "result": "Perfect! My implementation is complete. Let me create a summary of the changes:\n\n## Summary of Implementation\n\nI've successfully implemented the `--threshold` feature for `frai eval` that allows CI pipelines to fail when metrics are below specified minimums. Here's what was implemented:\n\n### **Core Changes (frai-core/src/eval/index.js)**\n- Added `validateThresholds()`: Validates threshold format and ensures metric IDs are known\n- Added `checkThresholds()`: Checks if metric scores meet their minimum thresholds\n- Updated `generateReport()`: Accepts optional `thresholds` parameter and adds `passed` and `thresholds` fields to reports\n\n### **Reporter Changes (frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js)**\n- Updated `toMarkdown()`: Adds \"Thresholds\" section showing PASS/FAIL status for each threshold\n\n### **CLI Changes (frai-cli/src/index.ts)**\n- Added `threshold?: string[]` to `EvalOptions` interface\n- Added `parseThresholds()`: Parses `<metric>=<number>` strings and validates format/values\n- Updated `runEvalCommand()`: \n  - Parses threshold options\n  - Passes thresholds to `generateReport()`\n  - Exits with code 1 if any threshold fails\n  - Exits with code 2 for invalid thresholds\n- Updated eval command: Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option (can be specified multiple times)\n\n### **Test Coverage (frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js)**\nAdded 6 comprehensive tests:\n1. \u2705 Validates and rejects unknown metrics\n2. \u2705 Validates and rejects invalid values (outside 0-1 range)\n3. \u2705 Passes when all metrics exceed minimums\n4. \u2705 Fails when a metric is below minimum  \n5. \u2705 Fails when metric has no score (null)\n6. \u2705 Works correctly without thresholds (backward compatible)\n\n### **Test Results**\n```\n\u2705 8 passed in eval tests (includes 3 original + 6 new)\n\u2705 34 total tests passed in frai-core\n\u274c 2 pre-existing failures (unrelated - governance test + toxicity metric issue)\n```\n\n### **Behavior**\n- **Exit 0**: All thresholds pass or no thresholds specified\n- **Exit 1**: One or more thresholds fail\n- **Exit 2**: Malformed threshold or unknown metric ID (with helpful error message listing valid metrics)\n- **Report**: Written either way with threshold results included\n\nAll new functionality is backward compatible - without `--threshold`, behavior is identical to before.",
